        "https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-synlet/bioconductor-synlet_2.10.0_src_all.tar.gz" ;
    schema1:identifier "biotools:synlet" ;
    schema1:license "GPL-3" ;
    schema1:name "bioconductor-synlet" ;
    schema1:softwareVersion "2.10.0" ;
    schema1:url "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/synlet.html" .

bioconda:bioconductor-systempiper a schema1:SoftwareApplication ;
    schema1:alternateName "systemPipeR: Workflow Environment for Data Analysis and Report Generation" ;
    schema1:description "systemPipeR is a multipurpose data analysis workflow environment that unifies R with command-line tools. It enables scientists to analyze many types of large- or small-scale data on local or distributed computer systems with a high level of reproducibility, scalability and portability. At its core is a command-line interface (CLI) that adopts the Common Workflow Language (CWL). This design allows users to choose for each analysis step the optimal R or command-line software. It supports both end-to-end and partial execution of workflows with built-in restart functionalities. Efficient management of complex analysis tasks is accomplished by a flexible workflow control container class. Handling of large numbers of input samples and experimental designs is facilitated by consistent sample annotation mechanisms. As a multi-purpose workflow toolkit, systemPipeR enables users to run existing workflows, customize them or design entirely new ones while taking advantage of widely adopted data structures within the Bioconductor ecosystem. Another important core functionality is the generation of reproducible scientific analysis and technical reports. For result interpretation, systemPipeR offers a wide range of plotting functionality, while an associated Shiny App offers many useful functionalities for interactive result exploration. The vignettes linked from this page include (1) a general introduction, (2) a description of technical details, and (3) a collection of workflow templates." ;
    schema1:downloadUrl "https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/systemPipeR_2.16.3.tar.gz",
        "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/Archive/systemPipeR/systemPipeR_2.16.3.tar.gz",
        "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/systemPipeR_2.16.3.tar.gz",
        "https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-systempiper/bioconductor-systempiper_2.16.3_src_all.tar.gz" ;
    schema1:identifier "biotools:systempiper" ;
    schema1:license "Artistic-2.0" ;
    schema1:name "bioconductor-systempiper" ;
    schema1:softwareVersion "2.16.3" ;
    schema1:url "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/systemPipeR.html" .

bioconda:bioconductor-targetscore a schema1:SoftwareApplication ;
    schema1:alternateName "TargetScore: Infer microRNA targets using microRNA-overexpression data and sequence information" ;
    schema1:citation "doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btt599" ;
    schema1:description "Infer the posterior distributions of microRNA targets by probabilistically modelling the likelihood microRNA-overexpression fold-changes and sequence-based scores. Variaitonal Bayesian Gaussian mixture model (VB-GMM) is applied to log fold-changes and sequence scores to obtain the posteriors of latent variable being the miRNA targets. The final targetScore is computed as the sigmoid-transformed fold-change weighted by the averaged posteriors of target components over all of the features." ;
    schema1:downloadUrl "https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/TargetScore_1.48.0.tar.gz",
        "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/Archive/TargetScore/TargetScore_1.48.0.tar.gz",
        "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/TargetScore_1.48.0.tar.gz",
        "https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-targetscore/bioconductor-targetscore_1.48.0_src_all.tar.gz" ;
    schema1:identifier "biotools:targetscore" ;
    schema1:license "GPL-2" ;
    schema1:name "bioconductor-targetscore" ;
    schema1:softwareVersion "1.48.0" ;
    schema1:url "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/TargetScore.html" .

bioconda:bioconductor-tcgabiolinks a schema1:SoftwareApplication ;
    schema1:alternateName "TCGAbiolinks: An R/Bioconductor package for integrative analysis with GDC data" ;
    schema1:citation "doi:10.1093/nar/gkv1507" ;
    schema1:description "The aim of TCGAbiolinks is : i) facilitate the GDC open-access data retrieval, ii) prepare the data using the appropriate pre-processing strategies, iii) provide the means to carry out different standard analyses and iv) to easily reproduce earlier research results. In more detail, the package provides multiple methods for analysis (e.g., differential expression analysis, identifying differentially methylated regions) and methods for visualization (e.g., survival plots, volcano plots, starburst plots) in order to easily develop complete analysis pipelines." ;
    schema1:downloadUrl "https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/TCGAbiolinks_2.38.0.tar.gz",
